# Referral Platform — Cursor Rules
# Always read this file before starting any task.
# Also read SPEC.md and PROGRESS.md before starting any feature work.

---

## Project Overview
This is a white-label referral-as-a-service platform with a shell app and casual games.
- Users earn credits by referring friends who engage with games
- Credits cash out as real USD via Stripe Connect
- Single-tenant first (one game), multi-tenant later

---

## Tech Stack
- Framework: Next.js 15 (App Router)
- Language: TypeScript (strict mode — no `any`)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4
- Database: Supabase (Postgres)
- Auth: Supabase Auth
- Hosting: Vercel
- Email: Resend
- Payouts: Stripe Connect
- Rate limiting: Upstash Redis
- IDE: Cursor with Claude

---

## Monorepo Structure
```
referral/
├── apps/
│   ├── shell/        ← shell/test client (Next.js)
│   └── game-1/       ← first game (Next.js, added later)
├── packages/
│   └── api/          ← shared referral backend & API routes
├── SPEC.md           ← full project specification (source of truth)
├── PROGRESS.md       ← what's done, what's next, known issues
└── .cursorrules      ← this file
```

---

## Golden Rules (follow every single time)
1. Always read `.cursorrules`, `SPEC.md`, and `PROGRESS.md` before starting any feature.
2. Every Cursor task must end with: `Commit and push to [branch-name] and open a PR.`
3. This is a code change task only — do not investigate or research.
4. Never use `any` in TypeScript. Always type everything explicitly.
5. Always mark optional fields with `?` — do not assume all fields are required.
6. Never duplicate logic that already exists — find and import it instead.
7. Always use the `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` (not the anon key) for server-side API routes.
8. **IMPORTANT:** Supabase SQL migrations must be run MANUALLY in the Supabase SQL editor before merging any PR that includes schema changes. Cursor cannot do this automatically.

---

## Branch Naming
- Features: `feat/short-description`
- Bug fixes: `fix/short-description`
- Database changes: `db/short-description`

---

## API Conventions
- All API routes live under `/api/v1/`
- All endpoints require authentication unless explicitly marked public
- All responses follow: `{ success: boolean, data?: any, error?: string }`
- Idempotency keys must be included for all credit/cashout operations

---

## Supabase Conventions
- Never bypass Row Level Security (RLS) from the client
- Use service role key only in server-side API routes
- All DB changes go through migration files — never edit schema manually in dashboard
- Remind Tony to run migrations in Supabase SQL editor before merging

---

## TypeScript Conventions
- Use `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/intersections
- All API request/response types must be defined in `packages/api/types/`
- No implicit returns — always return explicitly

---

## Credits & Finance Rules (from SPEC.md)
- 100 credits = $1 USD (fixed exchange rate, stored in admin config)
- Minimum cashout: 1,000 credits ($10)
- All cashouts >= 10,000 credits ($100) go to UNDER_REVIEW automatically
- Never apply exchange rate changes retroactively

---

## Cursor Command Template
Use this structure for every task you give Cursor:

```
Read .cursorrules, SPEC.md, and PROGRESS.md first. This is a code change task only.

On branch [branch-name], [describe the change]:

1. [Specific change #1 — file, location, what to do]
2. [Specific change #2]

[Any constraints or rules to follow]

After completing, update PROGRESS.md to reflect what was done.
Commit and push to [branch-name] and open a PR.
```
